{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KKMo7pFmd8yAB62Ab7nZtX","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, the technique proposed was **shifting to positive space using the formula `Long.MAX_VALUE - sourceProducerId - 1`**.\\\\n\\\\nThis was identified in the critical KIP-1279 (Cluster Mirroring) discussion as a solution to the PID formula bug (VK4 & VK8 - Transactional Integrity & PID Formula Bug). The original formula `-(PID + 2)` was producing negative numbers, which failed the `hasProducerId()` validity check that requires values to be greater than -1. The proposed solution uses this bitwise shift approach to keep producer IDs in positive space while tracking mirrored source producer IDs in memory for LSO calculation at the destination broker.\\\\n\\\\n**Source**: `/store/discussions/kip-1279-cluster-mirroring.md`, line 32\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1279-cluster-mirroring.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":19.68,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":76131,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":8048,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0309421,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1435}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5cec55d2-d34b-4c62-8f2b-91f2d15d42c0","uuid":"974ccad5-a223-41df-984a-f878eccb1c47","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:46:38.353Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, the technique proposed was **shifting to positive space using the formula `Long.MAX_VALUE - sourceProducerId - 1`**.\\\\n\\\\nThis was identified in the critical KIP-1279 (Cluster Mirroring) discussion as a solution to the PID formula bug (VK4 & VK8 - Transactional Integrity & PID Formula Bug). The original formula `-(PID + 2)` was producing negative numbers, which failed the `hasProducerId()` validity check that requires values to be greater than -1. The proposed solution uses this bitwise shift approach to keep producer IDs in positive space while tracking mirrored source producer IDs in memory for LSO calculation at the destination broker.\\\\n\\\\n**Source**: `/store/discussions/kip-1279-cluster-mirroring.md`, line 32\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1279-cluster-mirroring.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":19.68,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":76131,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":8048,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0309421,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1435}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, the technique proposed was **shifting to positive space using the formula `Long.MAX_VALUE - sourceProducerId - 1`**.\\n\\nThis was identified in the critical KIP-1279 (Cluster Mirroring) discussion as a solution to the PID formula bug (VK4 & VK8 - Transactional Integrity & PID Formula Bug). The original formula `-(PID + 2)` was producing negative numbers, which failed the `hasProducerId()` validity check that requires values to be greater than -1. The proposed solution uses this bitwise shift approach to keep producer IDs in positive space while tracking mirrored source producer IDs in memory for LSO calculation at the destination broker.\\n\\n**Source**: `/store/discussions/kip-1279-cluster-mirroring.md`, line 32\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"store\",\"discussions/kip-1279-cluster-mirroring.md\"],\"seconds\":19.68,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":1,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":76131,\"cache_write_tokens\":8048,\"cost_usd\":0.0309421,\"input_tokens\":58,\"output_tokens\":1435}}"}}}
